    <div class="Wolfe">
    <img src="https://www.silive.com/resizer/v2/EIFGOVCJWJGRHJDKCXZ4G564TE.jpg?auth=d6fa2ee21c823caaa2b66796653978dd14dc328a2264a5554c1c236807ae6d19&width=1280&smart=true&quality=90" alt="Wolfe's Pond">
    </div>
        <p> Wolfe’s Pond Beach is a quiet, tucked‑away shoreline on Staten Island’s southern edge, offering a very different vibe from the larger, busier NYC beaches. It’s often described as one of the city’s least‑crowded beaches, sitting along Raritan Bay and Prince’s Bay inside Wolfe’s Pond Park. The beach faces sheltered bay waters rather than the open Atlantic, which gives it a calmer, more intimate feel. Visitors highlight its natural setting, with seaweed, marine life, and a more rugged shoreline compared to places like South Beach or Midland Beach. The surrounding park adds miles of walking paths, forested areas, ponds, and recreation spaces, making it a great spot for a mix of beach time and nature exploration. While it’s not a classic boardwalk-style beach, Wolfe’s Pond Beach is appreciated for being a quiet escape, ideal for low-key sunbathing, peaceful walks, and enjoying a less commercial slice of NYC’s  </p>
